# System Monitor App

A terminal-based, real-time system monitoring tool built with Node.js. It displays live stats for CPU, memory, disk, network, and top processes — all rendered directly in your terminal with colorful progress bars and intuitive keyboard navigation.

---

## Features

- **CPU Usage** — Per-core usage with progress bars, average usage, and load averages (1m / 5m / 15m)
- **Memory Usage** — Total, used, and free RAM with a visual progress bar
- **Disk Usage** — Usage stats for the root partition (`/`)
- **Network Stats** — Real-time download and upload speeds
- **Top Processes** — Top 5 CPU-consuming processes with user, CPU%, MEM%, and command name
- **Color-coded Metrics** — Green (< 50%), Yellow (< 75%), Red (>= 75%)
- **Scrollable UI** — Navigate content taller than the terminal window
- **Live Updates** — Refreshes every 1 second

---

## Prerequisites

- [Node.js](https://nodejs.org/) v18 or higher (ESM support required)
- Linux OS (uses `/proc/net/dev` for network stats and `ps`/`df` commands)

---

## Installation

1. Clone the repository or download the project files.

2. Install dependencies:

```bash
npm install
```

---

## Usage

```bash
node app.js
```

The monitor will launch in the terminal's alternate buffer (your previous terminal content is preserved on exit).

---

## Keyboard Controls

| Key                  | Action                        |
|----------------------|-------------------------------|
| `↑` / `k`            | Scroll up one line            |
| `↓` / `j`            | Scroll down one line          |
| `Page Up`            | Scroll up 10 lines            |
| `Page Down`          | Scroll down 10 lines          |
| `Home`               | Jump to top                   |
| `End`                | Jump to bottom                |
| `Ctrl + C`           | Exit the monitor              |

